                                        "sense_id": "3a9f622f-57f1-3968-92b9-3480b10332d4",
                                        "entry_id": "66f12170-adf9-35af-89d9-9e0ce1e6d1b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The title of a king."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48732cd1-d19b-4558-aaa5-c013f90ea620",
                                                "sense_id": "3a9f622f-57f1-3968-92b9-3480b10332d4",
                                                "text": "As we climbed the Marykirk Bank Ogilvie spoke of the passes leading over to Deeside, and of the Royal deer forests around Balmoral; then, with mingled pride and modesty, he added, \"I've driven the King seven times.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca69b911-243f-4557-9849-859bdcb84ec1",
                                                "sense_id": "3a9f622f-57f1-3968-92b9-3480b10332d4",
                                                "text": "One, a grant by Archbishop Wulfred to that community, is datable to 825x32; while the other two (both copies of the same document) record an agreement between Archbishop Ceolnoth and Kings Egbert and Æthelwulf which was enacted in 838."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "King",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5d32fbf-6719-39f0-89af-7e9880ffe592",
                                        "entry_id": "5bcf3e53-e62a-30d8-91b5-e24a05a594b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An English and Scottish surname transferred from the nickname, originally a nickname for someone who either acted as if he were a king or had worked in the king's household."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc985512-11e4-4df6-8bab-68a23fc2f298",
                                                "sense_id": "b5d32fbf-6719-39f0-89af-7e9880ffe592",
                                                "text": "The Russians clinched the victory when Vera Zvonareva rallied to defeat Vania King, 4-6, 6-3, 6-2, in the first reverse singles match, giving her team a 3-0 lead. […] After Russia went ahead, 3-0, Ahsha Rolle defeated Elena Vesnina, 6-3, 6-4, then King paired with Liezel Huber to beat Vesnina and Svetlana Kuznetsova, 7-6 (3), 6-4, in the doubles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef8710d4-1be1-433c-a7a4-335b641add20",
                                                "sense_id": "b5d32fbf-6719-39f0-89af-7e9880ffe592",
                                                "text": "So when King – who had been in Atlanta for “Bloody Sunday” – telegrammed Parks about returning to Alabama to take part in a third mass march from Selma to Montgomery, her immediate answer was “Why, of course.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed05e818-c5c0-3bcf-a4ac-a1fd52dbd2c8",
                                        "entry_id": "5bcf3e53-e62a-30d8-91b5-e24a05a594b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "King class, a class of steam locomotives once used on the GWR."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
